    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072906
    m_Localized: Beautifies adjacent tiles and can also be harvested for wood and
      saplings.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072907
    m_Localized: Beautifies adjacent tiles and can also be harvested for wood and
      saplings.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072908
    m_Localized: Provides storage slots and shortens material transport distance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072909
    m_Localized: Farms can select a crop and consume seed to sow it. Growth requires
      enough workers, sustained full staffing improves the harvest, and automatic
      harvesting and replanting can be enabled.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072910
    m_Localized: The fishing hut produces fish periodically and can yield rare catches
      once adequately staffed. This building is not yet fully implemented.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072911
    m_Localized: The granary provides low-loss food-storage slots. Upgrades, sufficient
      workers, and maintenance expand capacity and build experience, while full staffing
      can unlock bonus slots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072912
    m_Localized: A hospital's level and current staffing expand its medical coverage
      and strength. Proper maintenance and sufficient workers also build operational
      experience for upgrades.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072913
    m_Localized: The Land Expedition Office forms teams from assigned workers. Teams
      can depart once staffing and level requirements are met; full staffing improves
      item yields, and successful expeditions build upgrade experience.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072914
    m_Localized: The logging hut employs workers to produce logs periodically. Actual
      output depends on current staffing and maintenance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072915
    m_Localized: When fully staffed, the market becomes a resource supply point and
      records the value of goods handled this turn, converting a share into Gold
      at the end of the turn.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072916
    m_Localized: The Royal Palace is the settlement's central building, providing
      a fixed population, storage slots, and research points while also serving as
      an important resource supply node.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072917
    m_Localized: A police station's level and current staffing expand its security
      coverage and strength. Proper maintenance and sufficient workers also build
      operational experience for upgrades.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072918
    m_Localized: A quarry must fully cover a land-based stone deposit. Once staffed
      and maintained, it produces stone periodically, and upgrades significantly
      increase output.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072919
    m_Localized: Residences sustain population growth through diet and quality of
      life and generate tax revenue periodically. Higher levels can house more residents.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072920
    m_Localized: A dirt road reduces the action-point cost of crossing its tile,
      improving connections and transport efficiency within the settlement.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072921
    m_Localized: Once built, a statue beautifies orthogonally adjacent tiles. The
      Goddess and Sacred Deer skins change only its appearance, not its costs or
      gameplay.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072922
    m_Localized: Double-click to attempt to collect 10 Dirt. A use is consumed only
      when the inventory can accept the full amount, and the resource node disappears
      after three successful collections.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072923
    m_Localized: Double-click to attempt to collect 10 Stone. A use is consumed only
      when the inventory can accept the full amount, and the resource node disappears
      after three successful collections.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15044556432072924
    m_Localized: Once operational, it beautifies orthogonally adjacent tiles. Double-click
      to harvest it; resources are granted when its durability is depleted or it
      is demolished.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
